Stress At pivot points and hinges:
Max Stress was mostly seen around these points only, 
both hinges for the spring and the throwing arm were reinforced and were made of high strength steel to deal with high stress.

Bending in primary structural member:
Bending was seen in the throwing are during the peak launch load, slight bending was also seen during impact.
During peak load, max displacement was seen in the load holding cup's edge which was 3.365mm and min was 0mm.
During impact, max displacement was seen in the load holding cup's edge which was 2.285mm and min was 0mm.

Regions of stress concentration:
During Peak load: Most stress was concentrated in the pivots and hinges, max stress was in the hinge holding the spring to the base which was around 112MPa.
                  Some stress concentration was also seen in the lower throwing arm.
During Impact: Most stress is concentrated at the neck of the throwing arm which is attached to the cup, nost certainly because of the inertia of the cup.

Overall factor of safety:
During peak load: Minimum factor of safety was 3.066 which is well above the standard 2
During impact: Minimum factor of safety was 2.447 which is well above the standard 2
